WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.844
The implementation track teaches the
same estate from the engineer's chair,

2
00:00:04.844 --> 00:00:09.562
in ten build modules from D N S and
address management to day-two operations.

3
00:00:09.562 --> 00:00:13.773
The order is a real dependency
chain: address before you identify,

4
00:00:13.773 --> 00:00:18.296
identify before you shape transport,
transport before you place data,

5
00:00:18.296 --> 00:00:21.337
and certificates before
the network enforces.

6
00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:24.154
Devices, the cloud platform and security

7
00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:27.550
operations run in parallel
once identity exists.

8
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.300
Day two comes last, because it
runs what everything else built.

9
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.488
Every module ends the same way.

10
00:00:33.488 --> 00:00:37.950
Done means it works and its evidence has
landed where an assessor can read it.

11
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:43.258
Every lab teaches three habits: observe
before you enforce, with report-only,

12
00:00:43.258 --> 00:00:47.807
monitor and shadow modes; keep a
way back in, with emergency access

13
00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:52.188
accounts created first; and export
the record, not a screenshot.

14
00:00:52.188 --> 00:00:56.038
Certifications are examples,
not proof, and they change.

15
00:00:56.038 --> 00:01:04.438
Microsoft retired AZ-500 on August
31, 2026, and SC-500 replaced it.

16
00:01:04.438 --> 00:01:08.590
So the program re-checks its
certification table at every gate.
